===Etymology===
{{PIE root|de|keh₂p}}
From {{inh|de|goh|habēn}} (Akin to {{cog|osx|hebbian}}, {{cog|non|hafa}} ({{cog|sv|hava}}/{{m|sv|ha}}), {{cog|ofs|habba}}, {{cog|got|𐌷𐌰𐌱𐌰𐌽}}, {{cog|ang|habban}}), from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*habjaną}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*keh₂p-||to grasp}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|hebben}}, {{cog|en|have}}, {{cog|da|have}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhaːbən/|[ˈhaːbən]|[ˈhaːbm̩]|lang=de}} {{a|standard}}
* {{IPA|/ham/|lang=de}} {{a|common; particularly in the present tense, occasionally also in the infinitive}}
* {{audio|De-haben.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-irregular|hat|hatte|gehabt|past subjunctive=hätte}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[have]]; to [[possess]], to [[own]]
# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[have]]; to [[hold]], to [[contain]]
# {{lb|de|auxiliary|with a past participle}} to [[have]] {{non-gloss definition|forms the [[perfect tense|perfect]] and [[past perfect|past perfect tense]]}}
# {{lb|de|reflexive|colloquial}} to [[make a fuss]]
#: {{ux|de|Hab dich nicht so!|Don't make such a fuss!}}
# {{lb|de|colloquial|with {{m|de|es}} and {{m|de|mit}}}} to be occupied with, to like
#: {{ux|de|Ich '''hab''''s nich so mit [[Hund]]en.|I'm not a great fan of dogs.|lit=I don't '''have''' it that much with dogs.}}

